# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for tonight's four-card window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/serve-3 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Every value is final.
# ORDER.txt says the order, each job's image, its stop rule and its minutes. The image is tp4-serve-3 throughout: T1 builds it, the
# later jobs serve it, and a commit after T1's tag needs a new tag and every later job the new one.
# T5: a deliberate reproduction of v164 with instruments: c2-packed-tp4-diag (gate only): the audits-off environment of v164, the OLD
# tail narrowing (QWEN_FAST_BUDGET_CAP=0), the watchdog at 120 s, and the host-only instruments (QWEN_FAST_SEQ_STAGE_LOG,
# QWEN_FAST_TRACE_CENSUS, QWEN_FAST_CCL_HANDLE_LOG, QWEN_FAST_MEMORY_LEDGER_L1), so the device allocation sequence is v164's.
# The tests are v164's sequence up to its hang: concurrent4_v164order admits the four users in v164's order (8376, 7423, 452 and
# 533 tokens), so the pair [0, 1] trace is captured before the short-prompt engines are built.
# A localisation objective, not a service one. PASS (localised): a stall fires the watchdog within 120 s and the EngineCore log holds
# the last '[SEQ-STAGE] ... begin' line, the faulthandler stack naming the blocking call, that request's first-replay census line,
# the CCL indices and any '[PINDIAG] trace overlap' lines. PASS (not reproduced): every test completes; record 'old tail, audits off,
# completed once on tp4-serve-3' with the census of first narrow replays and any overlap lines (one layout outcome, not a
# qualification). INCONCLUSIVE: the engine stops without a watchdog dump (an uninterruptible PCIe wait).
# The last device job before the hand-back, so a wedge costs only T6's reset. Duration (estimate): 20 min. Not a stop job.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-3
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-diag
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,long_real_text,concurrent4_v164order,concurrent4_steady,replay_concurrent4
